# Write detailed git commit messages

## Detailed commit messages

Always write detailed git commit messages that span multiple lines.
Always use the correct syntax to handle multiple lines (git commit -m "Line 1" -m "Line 2" -m "Line 3").

## Prompt the user first

Do not attempt to make a git commit without first asking the user if they are satisfied with the implementation.